                <pb facs="0525" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24595/5.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Chargé
                    Monroe.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-05-17"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wilson informs the legation that the Red Cross proposes a further expenditure
                    of $2,500 for material for building shelters, to be shipped on May 24 from New
                    Orleans. Instructs legation to telegraph suggestions as to material, quality,
                    general dimensions, etc.</p>
            </div>
